{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2374514","formula":"C₁₄H₁₆BrNO₂","hill":"C14H16BrNO2","elements":["H","C","N","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":16.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"Brofaromine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Brofaromine (proposed brand name Consonar) is a reversible inhibitor of monoamine oxidase A (RIMA) discovered by Ciba-Geigy. The compound was primarily researched in the treatment of depression and anxiety but its development was dropped before it was brought to market. Brofaromine also acts as a serotonin reuptake inhibitor, and its dual pharmacologic effects offered promise in the treatment of a wide spectrum of depressed patients while producing less severe anticholinergic side effects in comparison with older standard drugs like certain of the tricyclic antidepressants."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":44571,"mass":310.19,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=CC(=C2C(=C1)C=C(O2)C3CCNCC3)Br","inchikey":"WZXHSWVDAYOFPE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4-(7-bromo-5-methoxy-1-benzofuran-2-yl)piperidine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"44571","atoms":34,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.215,"y":-3.397,"z":0.0,"el":"Br"},{"x":-0.481,"y":-0.643,"z":-0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":4.886,"y":0.352,"z":0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.186,"y":-0.355,"z":0.001,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.471,"y":0.747,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.116,"y":0.144,"z":1.26,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.118,"y":0.146,"z":-1.26,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.639,"y":0.261,"z":1.21,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.641,"y":0.264,"z":-1.208,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.964,"y":0.621,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.043,"y":1.546,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":1.254,"y":0.804,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.877,"y":-0.535,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":2.625,"y":1.116,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":1.776,"y":-1.6,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":3.553,"y":0.066,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":3.134,"y":-1.2